hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"387","It is narrated by Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, it is narrated by Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Aoun, and he is ibn Abi Juhayfah, on the authority of his father, he said: “I saw Bilal gives the call to prayer and he follows it with his mouth,” and Sufyan described: He tilted his head to the right and to the left. Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani narrated to us, Ishaq bin Yusuf Al-Azraq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Aoun bin Abi Juhayfah, on the authority of Abu Juhayfah, he said: I witnessed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Al-Bathaa, who was in a red hood, and he was with people, walking. Then Bilal came and gave the call to prayer, then he turned around to follow his mouth. Here, what he means by saying: “Hayat al-Salat” (Hayat al-Salat), “Hayat al-Falah” (Hayat al-Falah). Wakee’ said, on the authority of Al-Thawri in this report: So he started saying this in his call to prayer, and turning his head, right and left, greeting Al-Falah. Salam bin Junada narrated it, saying: Waki` narrated to us."
